  "reason": "The current best (config_033, acc=0.713) uses scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer + weighted fusion + resnet50. The image-only resnet50 baseline was very weak (0.208), yet it still contributed meaningfully in the multimodal setting (0.713 vs 0.653 RNA-only). The most impactful untested variable is whether a stronger image encoder (ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L) can further boost the multimodal model. config_039 isolates exactly this: it swaps resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l while keeping all other settings at their empirically best values (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer, weighted). This is the single most informative next test because it directly extends the winning configuration along the one axis with the largest remaining uncertainty (image representation quality), and if it succeeds it sets a new best with one experiment still remaining for fine-tuning."
}

